Do not add `image.distribution` while generating the instance. The host adds
the immutable registry reference and digest only after the image passes
validation and is successfully pushed.

Omit `runtime.entrypoint` and `runtime.command` when the source image's normal
startup must run. When the intended fault prevents the target service from
starting, keep the benchmark container alive for investigation, for example:

```json
{
  "ready_check": "test -f /etc/mysql/conf.d/fault.cnf",
  "ready_timeout_seconds": 60,
  "entrypoint": "/bin/bash",
  "command": ["-lc", "exec tail -f /dev/null"]
}
```

The reproduction and F2P scripts must then start the real target service
themselves to observe the failure and repaired behavior.

